{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"agent_message","text":"I submitted the mitigation, but I did not find or fix a confirmed root cause. The submission is recorded (`stage: mitigation`), so the grade reflects the cluster state as it stands.\n\n**What I checked**\n- All 24 pods in `astronomy-shop` are Running with no restarts, and all services have endpoints.\n- Products, recommendations, cart, the homepage, and the LLM assistant route through `frontend-proxy` all answer in milliseconds.\n- Checkout is placing orders and sending confirmation emails.\n- All flagd flags are `off`, and flagd is reachable.\n\n**Remaining issues**\n- **`/api/shipping` on the frontend is failing.** It hung for 8–25 seconds on the direct and proxy paths, then returned 500 through the proxy. The `shipping` and `quote` services answer correctly when called directly, so the fault is inside the frontend's shipping handler. I couldn't read that code because the frontend image is distroless and no source is on the host.\n- **`orders-validator` is stuck.** The consumer in `orders-pipeline-scripts` paused at offset 20 on a malformed record (`Expecting value: line 1 column 35`). Lag on `orders-fulfillment` is about 100 and growing. Nothing on the user path consumes this topic, so I believe it isn't the cause of the user-facing degradation, but it is broken.\n- **Kafka CPU is high.** It was sustained at about 450m, and I didn't identify the cause.\n\n**Changes made**\n- Rolling restarts of `frontend`, `shipping`, `quote`, `currency`, `cart`, and `product-catalog`. These didn't clear the shipping failure. No manifests or config were changed.\n\n**Suggested next steps**\n- Check the frontend shipping route's logs or source for what it awaits, or redeploy the frontend from a known-good image.\n- Fix the `orders-validator` consumer to skip or dead-letter malformed records, then reset its offset."}}
